      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PINNIE (10) has been racing well and kept the ball rolling last week when she chased along the sprint lane to get within 2 metres of the winner. Strikes at 50 per cent at this longer distance including a win here three back. Strong claims. There was plenty to like about the fresh effort of KEAYANG STUKA (11) when he led and fought on for a 1.8m second last week, beating PINNIE home. Starts 10m behind her in the handicap but he hasn't missed a place in five second-up attempts, winning three. DARCYS FIREBALL (5) added to a string of wins and placings with a respectable third from this mark at his most recent appearance. Go well again. GET USED TO IT (9) hasn't raced for eight months but trialled well and is a two-time fresh winner. COURAGE STRIDE (8) switches form Sydney and could measure up.",
